# Testing rules

Write tests only after the user has approved tests for this task (AGENTS.md C7). Templates are in the `flutter-tests` skill.

- T1 HARD: Tests never touch the network, real storage, platform channels or wall-clock time. Replace these with fakes or mocks.
- T2 HARD: Don't change production code just to make a test pass. If a test exposes a real bug, report it.
- T3 SHOULD: Mirror `lib/` paths: `lib/features/x/data/repositories/x_repository_impl.dart` → `test/features/x/data/repositories/x_repository_impl_test.dart`.
- T4 SHOULD: Cover in this order:
  1. use cases and repositories (success and every failure path)
  2. Bloc/Cubit state sequences
  3. widget tests of the screen states (loading, error, empty, data)
  4. integration tests, only if asked
- T5 SHOULD: Use the mocking library already in `dev_dependencies`, and prefer small hand-written fakes for repositories. Ask before adding test packages (e.g. `bloc_test`).
- T6 SHOULD: One behavior per test, named `'<unit> <does what> when <condition>'`, with an arrange/act/assert structure.
- T7 SHOULD: Widget tests wrap the widget in the ancestors the app requires (theme, sizing and localization wrappers; see Project profile).
- T8 SHOULD: Run only the affected test files. Run the full suite when shared core code changed.
